<p class="disclaimer">Colors are our approximation of the late-1990s green-and-orange grocery look, not values sampled from Webvan’s brand guidelines, which we haven’t seen. The archived pages’ logo images weren’t captured.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="now">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head"><div class="sec-k"><span class="sn">15</span>Afterlife</div><h2 class="rv">What happened to everything</h2></div>
<div class="now-grid">
<div class="now rv"><div class="st">Oct 2001</div><h3>The warehouses</h3><p>Court-approved auctions of the equipment at ten facility sites and the Foster City headquarters.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-28">28</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st">Jul 2001</div><h3>The shareholders</h3><p>The company said it expected Nasdaq to delist the stock. Trading was halted the day of the shutdown.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-10">10</a></sup><sup class="fn"><a href="#src-13">13</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st">2009 – 2016</div><h3>The name</h3><p>Amazon bought the Webvan name and ran webvan.com as a store for non-perishable groceries, “part of the Amazon family.”<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-19">19</a></sup><sup class="fn"><a href="#src-20">20</a></sup><sup class="fn"><a href="#src-21">21</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st">2007 – today</div><h3>The idea</h3><p>AmazonFresh began testing in Seattle in 2007. Four Amazon grocery executives in 2013 were Webvan alumni.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-19">19</a></sup><sup class="fn"><a href="#src-20">20</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st">2012</div><h3>The robots</h3><p>Kiva Systems, founded by former Webvan logistics manager Mick Mountz, sold to Amazon for $775M.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-19">19</a></sup><sup class="fn"><a href="#src-23">23</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st">2022</div><h3>The alumni</h3><p>Doug Herrington, from Webvan’s executive team, became CEO of Worldwide Amazon Stores.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-22">22</a></sup></p></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

